{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ba325358f4deb9f8ed1b3d52ea759c75fbad266864b13f1e806fca7af3ac9390","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / batch runner","key_entities":["ProductionBatchRunner.run","run_pass1","shed_to_budget","plan_budget_cap","coverage[\"budget\"]","cap_source","REBAR_PLAN_REVIEW_BUDGET","req.usd_budget","budget_override_applied","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","src/rebar/production_batch_runner.py"],"problem_keywords":["budget cap override","pass1 parameter threading","seam injection","centrality scaling","cap verbatim"],"propositions":["run_pass1 and shed_to_budget lack an explicit cap_override parameter to thread through from ProductionBatchRunner.run, so req.usd_budget cannot be applied as a true cap override","plan_budget_cap computes the cap internally with centrality scaling, making REBAR_PLAN_REVIEW_BUDGET an env var base rather than a verbatim cap override, which defeats the purpose of a per-request budget override","coverage[\"budget\"] must track whether the cap came from an override or was computed, via a new cap_source field","An explicit cap_override of 0.0 must be honourable and not treated as falsy/absent, requiring selection on 'is None' not falsiness","The plan-review gate YAML currently sets no usd_budget on its finders batch, so live behaviour must remain unchanged until a separate cost-policy decision adds one"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787318358241943001,"uuid":"43ec9ca5-9109-4e11-9541-12381b07b1c3"}